  "narrative": {
    "intro": "This ranking lists the top small-business government contractors by contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Total obligations across the listed small businesses equal $21.5B. ATLANTIC DIVING SUPPLY, INC. leads the list with $2.9B in obligations. CSI AVIATION, INC follows with $1.1B. The next eight firms reported obligations between $916M and $611M, with AMERICAN CENTRIFUGE OPERATING, LLC at $916M, GENERAL MATTER, INC. at $900M, W S DARLEY & CO at $889M, THUNDERCAT TECHNOLOGY, LLC at $752M, FOUR POINTS TECHNOLOGY, L.L.C. at $717M, MINBURN TECHNOLOGY GROUP, LLC at $694M, COCHRANE USA INC at $641M, and ANDURIL INDUSTRIES, INC. at $611M. Readers should note that FY2026 totals are fiscal year to date and therefore partial. Use these figures as a snapshot of obligations so far in FY2026 rather than as full-year results. The list focuses strictly on contract obligations and ranks firms by the dollar value of obligations reported in FY2026 to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top small-business government contractors in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "ATLANTIC DIVING SUPPLY, INC. is first with $2.9B in obligations. CSI AVIATION, INC is second with $1.1B. AMERICAN CENTRIFUGE OPERATING, LLC through ANDURIL INDUSTRIES, INC. occupy ranks three through ten with obligations ranging from $916M to $611M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What does the $21.5B total represent?",
        "body": "The $21.5B total represents aggregate contract obligations to the listed small businesses for FY2026 to date. The total is a fiscal year to date figure and therefore reflects partial-year obligations, not full-year totals."
      }
    ]
  },
